## 11. Definition of done — “complete landing”

### 11.1 Engineering complete (current target met)

```text
[x] PR-0..3
[x] 4 blocks + smoke + guards
[ ] cutover denali.club on main
```

### 11.2 Product complete (competitive)

```text
[ ] PR-4 visual ≥7/10  → **done 2026-07-04**
[ ] PR-5 header + FAQ + footer  → **done 2026-07-04**
[ ] PR-6 why + journey + testimonials  → **done 2026-07-04**
[ ] PR-7 discovery (categories OR destinations minimum one)  → **done 2026-07-04**
[ ] PR-8 gallery OR blog + Lighthouse CI  → **done 2026-07-04** (gallery + equipment + skip + JSON-LD + Lighthouse `/`; blog stub gated off)
[ ] No fake stats audit pass
[ ] urban minimal unchanged (SMK-MKT-HOME-05)
[ ] Mobile 375px no overflow-x
```

### 11.3 Score rubric (updated)

| Score | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| 8.5/10 | Today — engineering MVP |
| 7/10 visual | PR-4 done |
| 8/10 product | PR-5 + PR-6 |
| 9/10 product | PR-7 discovery live |
| 10/10 | PR-8 + Lighthouse CI + cutover + real hero per tenant |

---

## 12. Industry alignment (research summary)

Sources: outdoor/tour landing guides (2025–2026) — hero outcome-led copy, trust below hero, FAQ near CTA, sticky mobile book, real photos, 200–750 words scannable, no hidden pricing on tour pages.

**Adopted into plan:** hero storytelling, FAQ, footer, testimonials, sticky CTA, scannable cards.  
**Rejected:** fake review counts, immersive scroll-only sites, skill-suggested navy palette.

